"""Bitcoin Vibes console.

A local web console for a Bitcoin Core fork whose operator changes it in plain
words. A coding agent (the `claude` CLI) proposes the change in an isolated
copy of the source. The console compiles the proposal inside an operating-
system sandbox, runs it beside an unmodified node on a throwaway private
chain, and shows the operator what each node made of the other's blocks. Only
then is the operator asked whether to keep it.

Standard library only. Binds to 127.0.0.1 and requires an access key for every
request, so other web pages cannot drive the node.
"""

